The development work will be organized around four primary roles: Student, Instructor,
Super User, and Administrator. The following module groups describe the intended coverage. They
do not imply that every feature will be available on every application; availability will follow the
role permissions and documented release scope.
Student Modules and Features
Academic Learning Features
• Course enrollment through valid join codes;
• Enrolled-course workspaces and learning materials;
• Supported document viewing, highlighting, and sticky-note annotation;
• Assignment submission and deadline access;
• Git-integrated repository submissions for applicable computing coursework;
• CodeLab programming execution and submission against predefined test cases;
• Personal grade viewing and descriptive visual grade analytics;
• Academic progress summaries based on available records.
Productivity and Study Features
• Personal notes and task management;
• Academic calendar with authorized saved events and coursework deadlines;
• Private note–event snapshot conversion;
• Digital flashcard creation and review;
• Configured review and mastery records;
• Focus study timers and study-session tracking.
Student Engagement Features
• Experience Points (EXP) and level progression;
• Achievements and badges;
• Daily streaks and department leaderboards;

• Applicable rewards and optional grade incentives, subject to academic rules.
Collaborative Learning Features
• Knowledge Exchange questions and answers;
• Academic and technical resource sharing;
• Contribution-related reputation points, maintained separately from EXP;
• Access to Faculty-Verified Answers.
Communication and Support Features
• Authorized announcements and relevant academic notifications;
• In-app help chatbot for navigation and platform assistance.
Instructor Modules and Features
Course and Learning Management
• Course and section creation and management;
• Course enrollment and join-code management;
• Learning-material organization;
• Assignment creation and deadline management;
• Repository-based submission review;
• CodeLab problem, activity, and predefined-test-case management.
Assessment and Grading
• Dynamic Gradebook and configurable component weights;
• Score recording and automatic grade computation;
• Student-performance analytics from available records;
• CSV grade export for authorized courses.

Student Engagement Management
• Instructor management of applicable rewards;
• Review of permitted participation and leaderboard information;
• Supported optional grade-incentive configuration under academic rules.
Collaborative Learning and Communication
• Knowledge Exchange moderation and answer verification;
• Configured reputation-management actions;
• Course announcements and relevant notification broadcasting.
Academic Coordination and Assessment Controls
• Weekly course schedules and effective-dated revisions;
• Permitted future class cancellation, rescheduling, and restoration;
• Authorized calendar events and audience-targeted communication;
• Defined coordination responsibilities attached to eligible Program Head accounts;
• Submission validation and applicable deadline restrictions;
• Supported assessment-event indicators for contextual instructor review.
Super User Modules and Features
Academic Oversight
• Web-based academic operations hub and permitted summaries;
• Faculty directory, organizational relationships, and program filters;
• Authorized timetable inspection;
• Restricted, read-only course supervision;
• Permitted academic-leadership assignments.
Academic Communication and Personal Organization
• Authorized shared faculty-announcement management;

• Audience-targeted academic events under the defined access rules;
• Owned private notes and events;
• Private note–event snapshot conversion.
Super User functions will remain separate from teaching, grading, assessment participation, and
generic system administration. Dean and Program Head designations will not automatically grant
permissions outside their defined coordination responsibilities.
Administrator Modules and Features
User and Access Management
• Student and Instructor account management;
• Registration approval and account-status management;
• Role and permission management;
• Instructor subject assignment;
• Super User account provisioning and revocation.
System Monitoring and Security
• System activity and administrative audit logs;
• Supported security-activity monitoring;
• Relevant user and IP activity information within the documented coverage.
Institutional and Academic Configuration
• Course and section directories;
• Department configuration and themes;
• Permitted faculty-directory and leadership configuration;
• Authorized schedule and class-exception management;
• Authorized shared-announcement management.

