An instructor respondent should:
1. Be an instructor affiliated with the Institute of Computing Studies of Colegio de Montalban;
2. Have prior experience using at least one Learning Management System (LMS) for teaching
or academic purposes;
3. Have a basic understanding of common LMS functions, such as course management,
learning material distribution, assignment management, grading, announcements, or student
monitoring;
4. Be willing to explore and use the implemented CdM LMS during the evaluation; and
5. Be willing to participate in the study.
An IT expert respondent should:
1. Have an academic degree, professional qualification, or relevant training in Information
Technology, Computer Science, Information Systems, Software Engineering, or a related
field;
2. Have relevant academic or professional experience in at least one area related to software
